WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.636
The Phoenix Pay System.

00:00:01.636 --> 00:00:05.215
Original budget: three hundred and nine million dollars.

00:00:05.215 --> 00:00:08.511
Final cost: two point two billion and climbing.

00:00:08.511 --> 00:00:12.465
One hundred and fifty thousand federal workers affected by pay errors.

00:00:12.465 --> 00:00:14.886
Some went months without a paycheque.

00:00:14.886 --> 00:00:19.420
Nine years in and a full replacement is not expected until 2031.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.840
Two hundred and sixteen thousand backlogged transactions.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:26.057
Recurring payroll glitches affecting pension calculations.

00:00:26.057 --> 00:00:30.136
Pay errors ranged from massive overpayments to complete non-payment.

00:00:30.136 --> 00:00:34.738
The Auditor General called the procurement a cautionary tale of failed government IT.

00:00:34.738 --> 00:00:36.774
Zero contractor accountability.

00:00:36.774 --> 00:00:38.829
No firm has been penalized.

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:40.863
No executive has been charged.

00:00:40.863 --> 00:00:47.113
The system that was supposed to save money has cost seven times its original estimate — and it still does not work.
